Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: the ambient light is averaged over two seconds

AutomaticBrightnessController believes a change of light only once both
its averages of the light sensor, over the last 2 and the last 10
seconds, have crossed the hysteresis threshold. On this phone the sensor
reports within a quarter of a second, but the ten-second average put 3
to 4 seconds between a change of light and the first move of the front
light (2026-11-10, the sensor's events against the brightness events).
The horizons come only from a display device config, which a GSI has
none of, so the constants are the phone's: 2 seconds and half a second.
The light moves about half a second after the light changes, and the
sensor's jitter of a lux at the dim end is still averaged out.
---
 .../com/android/server/display/DisplayDeviceConfig.java  | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayDeviceConfig.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayDeviceConfig.java
@@ -692,11 +692,11 @@
     private static final int INTERPOLATION_LINEAR = 1;
 
     // Length of the ambient light horizon used to calculate the long term estimate of ambient
-    // light.
-    private static final int AMBIENT_LIGHT_LONG_HORIZON_MILLIS = 10000;
+    // light. Kompakt: two seconds, not ten; the ten put 3 to 4 seconds before the front light moved.
+    private static final int AMBIENT_LIGHT_LONG_HORIZON_MILLIS = 2000;
 
     // Length of the ambient light horizon used to calculate short-term estimate of ambient light.
-    private static final int AMBIENT_LIGHT_SHORT_HORIZON_MILLIS = 2000;
+    private static final int AMBIENT_LIGHT_SHORT_HORIZON_MILLIS = 500;
 
     // Invalid value of AutoBrightness brightening and darkening light debounce
     private static final int INVALID_AUTO_BRIGHTNESS_LIGHT_DEBOUNCE = -1;
